            "review_title": "Review at Motsunabe Rakutenchi (Lau Long Bo Nhat Ban)",
            "review_text": "maryyeo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam4531 contributions\n0\nTasty tripe hotpot and wagyu barbeque... less crowded at 6pm!\nDec 2024 • Family\nThis chain is quite popular in Hakata/Fukuoka and has several outlets there, we missed our chance to try it there... coincidentally we found out that they also have an outlet in HCMC so we got to try it!\n\nWE LIKED THAT:\n- we can choose combo deals with both hotpot (tripe or chicken) and generous cuts of grilled wagyu, and we were surprised all combos had very good prices!\n- they have 8 types of authentic seasoning - we missed the Yuzukosho and Mentaiko flavours that we enjoyed in Fukuoka... and they have it here!\n- hubby likes tripes (low in fats but not so good for his cholesterol).. so it was good that there was plenty of chives in the hotpot (about 500 grams??) for real!\n- seasoned pork stomach appetizer was free, and staff would add rice and egg in hotpot at the end to make a porridge using the flavorful broth. Comforting ending.\n\nTIP:\nTry to reserve and visit early at around 6pm if you're visiting with family/ young ones, because this store is popular and it was full house by 7pm... can get a bit noisy and crowded with many customers celebrating with beer.\n\nLOCATION: \nThough it may look like a small dark alley to foreigners/tourists, but this street is in the famous \"little Japan town\" of HCMC. And while this shop is all the way at the corner (you have to pass by many parked motorbikes on this small alley). It is easy to remember that it is on the opposite end of Pizza 4Ps' first outlet in Vietnam.\n\nGlad we could try the authentic Motsunabe Rakutenchi in Vietnam.\nRead more\nWritten May 24, 2025",
